;##############################################################################
; WAR.EXE - The Ancient Art of War, CGA version (Broderbund; game (c) 1984 Dave and Barry Murry)
; From the 3.5" disk release (files dated 22 June 1989). Program copyright string: 1987.
;
; Annotated disassembly, generated by recursive descent from the program entry point,
; the overlay thunk table and every call target, so code and data are separated.
; Every code region is shown at the address it really runs at.
;
; Line format:   region:offset  file-offset  bytes  instruction   ; comment
;   region  rt = resident code (segment 0000), root = startup/loader (segment 028D),
;           ovl1..ovl7 = overlays (segment 0000, at their load offset), DS = data segment
;   Names in the form ovl3_4a2f / rt_1330 are unnamed functions; named ones are listed below.
;##############################################################################

;==============================================================================
; MZ HEADER
; file size          98304 bytes
; header             0x200 bytes, 71 relocations
; load image         0x30f0 bytes declared (file 0x200-0x32f0)
;                    the overlays and data segment are stored after it, inside WAR.EXE
; entry CS:IP        028D:02FA  (file 0x2dca)
; initial SS:SP      1381:0100
; linker             Phoenix Software PLINK86 (overlay loader "LINK86 Overlay Loader")
; file 0x17E20-end   zero padding
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; MEMORY MAP (segments relative to the load address)
; 0000:0000-28CF  rt     resident C code and library: file I/O, text, graphics, sound, game core
; 028D:0000-051D  root   startup and Phoenix overlay loader (entry 028D:02FA)
; 02DE:000E-017F  ldat   loader variables, PATH buffer, $-terminated loader messages
; 02F6:0000-008D  table  overlay descriptor table (16-byte entries, see below)
; 02F6:008E-0189  thunks 21 overlay call thunks, called as near calls 0000:2FEE + 12*n
; 0000:30F0-851F  ovl1   overlay area: overlay 1, or one of overlays 3-7 (all load at 30F0h)
; 0000:8520-8AFF  ovl2   overlay 2 (loads after overlay 1, so both can be resident)
; 08C6:0000-0B3F  DS     data segment DGROUP (initialised data, preloaded at startup)
; 08C6:0B40-....  DS     BSS, buffers, stack (SS=1381h); DGROUP ends at segment 1391h
;
; All game code (rt + overlays) runs with CS = load segment, so near calls between them work.
; Data references [xxxx] in this code are offsets in DS (segment 08C6h).
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; OVERLAY TABLE (file 0x3160, segment 02F6)
; #  file offset  size    loads at       flags  role
; 1  0x032f0     0x5430  030F-0852      0000   Main program: startup, title and menu screens, options (CNF), save/load, data disk, hardware detection, disk copy-protection check, byte-RLE picture loader
; 2  0x08720     0x05e0  0852-08B0      0001   Manual copy protection (WarW word list) and welcome message. Loads at 0852h, after overlay 1, so both can be resident together
; 3  0x08d00     0x1af0  030F-04BE      0000   Campaign editor: placing squads and flags (O1)
; 4  0x0a7f0     0x0ad0  030F-03BC      0000   Campaign editor: map maker (O0)
; 5  0x0b2c0     0x1690  030F-0478      0000   Formation editor, "Teach squads new formations" (O8 text, PL background)
; 6  0x0c950     0x5b70  030F-08C6      0000   Campaign play: the strategic map, movement, spies, messages (O5)
; 7  0x124c0     0x4e20  030F-07F1      0000   Battle screen: the fight between two squads (O6, O7, P0-PD backgrounds)
; 8  0x172e0     0x0b40  08C6-1391      4000   DGROUP initialised data (flag 4000h = load at startup)
;
; Entry layout (16 bytes, fields shared with the next entry): +4 flags (FFFFh ends the table,
; 4000h preload), +8 load segment, +A end segment, +C file-name pointer (WAR.EXE),
; +E file position in paragraphs; the size in paragraphs is at +2 of the next entry.
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; OVERLAY THUNKS (each: lcall 028D:02D0 / dw overlay# / jmp far target)
; thunk_00  0000:2FEE  -> overlay 1 at 30F0  ovl1_startup
; thunk_01  0000:2FFA  -> overlay 1 at 325F  game_init
; thunk_02  0000:3006  -> overlay 6 at 30F0  campaign_play
; thunk_03  0000:3012  -> overlay 7 at 30F0  battle
; thunk_04  0000:301E  -> overlay 1 at 35C4  save_game
; thunk_05  0000:302A  -> overlay 1 at 53AE  battle_report
; thunk_06  0000:3036  -> overlay 1 at 3D1E  campaign_menu
; thunk_07  0000:3042  -> overlay 1 at 4EB2  data_disk
; thunk_08  0000:304E  -> overlay 4 at 30F0  map_maker
; thunk_09  0000:305A  -> overlay 3 at 30F0  squads_editor
; thunk_10  0000:3066  -> overlay 1 at 3E08  campaign_intro
; thunk_11  0000:3072  -> overlay 1 at 4000  select_campaign
; thunk_12  0000:307E  -> overlay 5 at 30F0  formation_editor
; thunk_13  0000:308A  -> overlay 1 at 5782  options_shoppe
; thunk_14  0000:3096  -> overlay 1 at 39AA  show_scroll
; thunk_15  0000:30A2  -> overlay 1 at 389B  ensure_war_disk
; thunk_16  0000:30AE  -> overlay 1 at 3EB6  editor_menu
; thunk_17  0000:30BA  -> overlay 1 at 3FC3  ovl1_entry_3fc3
; thunk_18  0000:30C6  -> overlay 1 at 4808  choose_opponent
; thunk_19  0000:30D2  -> overlay 1 at 7EDA  init_hardware
; thunk_20  0000:30DE  -> overlay 2 at 8520  copy_protection
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; DATA FILES USED BY WAR.EXE (names are strings in DS)
; M         72 map tiles (32x20, CGA 2 bits/pixel); also used to check the WAR disk is present
;           (check_war_disk tries "B:M", "A:M", "M")
; CNF       saved options (load_file in ovl1_startup, save_options writes it)
; PM        title screen. PI title with barbarian. PJ opponents. PK Options Shoppe.
; PE, PF    parchment scrolls. PG, PH scene sheets for the menus. PN/PO battle report win/lose.
;           All loaded with load_picture_rle8 (overlay 1).
; P0-PD     battle backgrounds, chosen from the terrain (overlay 7, choose_battle_background).
; PL        formation editor background (overlay 5). Same word-RLE format as P0-PD.
; O0-O8     sprites and text for each module: O0 map maker (ovl4), O1 squads editor (ovl3),
;           O2 opponent bios, O3 story/rules/title steps, O4 menus (ovl1), O5 campaign
;           messages (ovl6), O6/O7 battle (ovl7), O8 formation editor (ovl5)
; T0-TA     campaigns, TITLES/DTITLES campaign lists (names built at run time)
; S         saved game (data disk, via make_data_path)
; TE        file used when preparing a data disk
; WarW      encrypted word list for the manual copy protection (overlay 2)
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; PICTURE FORMATS (decoded here)
; Word RLE (P0-PD, PL), decode_picture_rle16: two fields (even lines, then odd lines);
;   each field = word N, then N x [count byte, data word]; each field = 8000 bytes.
; Byte RLE (PE-PO), load_picture_rle8: pairs of [count, byte]; the pairs alternate
;   between the even-line field and the odd-line field until each has 8000 bytes.
; Both decode into an off-screen buffer (even lines at +0, odd lines at +3E80h),
;   then blit_buffer_to_cga copies it to video memory at B800h.
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; COPY PROTECTION
; 1. key_disk_check (overlay 1): reads track 10 of the original floppy with INT 13h,
;    including sector 241, which must fail with a CRC error, and compares 16 words.
; 2. copy_protection (overlay 2): loads WarW and asks "On page N, what is word N in
;    paragraph N" from the manual.
; The string "DPQZSJHIU 2:94 EBWF NVSSZ" is "COPYRIGHT 1983 DAVE MURRY" with each
; character +1.
;==============================================================================

;==============================================================================
; HARDWARE
; Video: CGA 320x200 mode 4 (detect_video also checks for Hercules). Palette set with
;        INT 10h AH=0Bh; AH=10h palette registers for PCjr/Tandy.
; Sound: PC speaker via PIT channel 2 (speaker_freq/on/off) and the Tandy/PCjr SN76489
;        chip at port C0h (tandy_sound).
; Input: keyboard (INT 16h), joystick (game port 201h, detect_joystick).
;==============================================================================

